{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310722,"nonce":"qBiFiRlF88o/E6P0HeRA+fnOuco=","title":"FIXED — switch-as-expression with constructor patterns silently SIGSEGVed for primitive-typed results because the desugar initialised the ...","message":"`var r = switch (v) { case A(x): x; case _: 0; };` SIGSEGVed for `r:Int`, but only as switch-as-expression — switch-as-statement was unaffected. Or-patterns like `case U8(x) | I8(x) | ... | I64(x): x` looked like \"or-pattern broken\" but were actually the same bug — `GGUFReader.metaInt`'s 8-way switch is what flagged it.\n\n\n`tast_to_hir::TypedExpressionKind::Switch` for the constructor-pattern path desugared:\n\n```haxe\nvar r = switch (v) {\n    case A(x): x;\n    case _:    0;\n};\n```\n\ninto\n\n```haxe\nvar r:Int = null;       // ← problem\nswitch (v) {\n    case A(x): r = x;\n    case _:    r = 0;\n}\n// continuation reads r\n```\n\nThe init expression was `HirExprKind::Null`, regardless of `result_type`. For primitive `result_type` (Int/Float/Bool), the MIR-level register for `r` got typed as `Ptr(_)` (the build_null lowering's natural type), but the case bodies stored i32/i64 into that slot. The continuation's `read r` then reinterpreted the slot as a pointer — clean SIGSEGV.\n\n\nPick a type-appropriate default for the temp:\n- `Int` → `HirLiteral::Int(0)`\n- `Float` → `HirLiteral::Float(0.0)`\n- `Bool` → `HirLiteral::Bool(false)`\n- otherwise → `HirExprKind::Null`\n\nThe continuation now reads the correctly-typed slot.\n\n\nWhen desugaring an expression into a temp + assignments + final read, the temp's init must match the result type's MIR register class. Don't reach for `null` as a universal default — only `Ptr`/`Optional` types tolerate it. Same caveat as `maybe_box_for_optional` and the binop unbox in [[bugs-null-arith-no-unbox]].\n\n\nRepro tests in `/tmp/or_field_inline.hx`, `/tmp/or_pattern_8way.hx`, and `/tmp/or_lit.hx` all now print correct values. nue's `GGUFReader.metaInt` works (was SIGILL before — the loader-side dispatch failed at the metaInt or-pattern). Haxe regression remains 128/128.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_switch_expr_null_init` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}